# Loop condition observes the element a previous iteration rewrote

Verifies the emitted loop condition uses the stored subtype rather than the
entry subtype. The body stores `2cm`, so the second test of `a[0] < 15mm` reads
`20mm` and ends the loop after one iteration instead of looping forever.

>>> source
let a: int[] = [10mm]
let n = 0

while (a[0] < 15mm) {
    n = n + 1
    a[0] = 2cm
}

print(n)

<<< stdout
1

<<< stderr
